{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED: LL-1 notes-only amendment at exact head ed0775f3a3a4c5e184b109c4f1d32e34f11c76b4, tree 47825257f6d4463caaa31fc3c0ad96930be1755e, over published main 12cb8fa7. The only changed path is notes/2026-11-10-live-level.md (artifact ba138bcc, which rests on promise 85c044fd and request 5fcd2b9b). Notes-only gate END e91c2230 passed. The log SHA-256 1fc3a523… matches the file. check-commit-messages flags 0 of 2 commits. The head merges cleanly onto origin/main, diff --check is clean, and the added lines name no other project or private path.\n\nRuling coverage (8568a680). Section 3.9 carries all four parts:\n1. The retry record is keyed by (actor, target item), and an open keys by the item it creates. The exact-retry, idempotency-mismatch and superseded-repeat answers match the ruling.\n2. Fixed hashes stop after seq 1, and the red-first witness test is an obligation of the source head.\n3. Final items are evicted together with their retry records. The answers for a read, an act and a leave retry name `no-item`, and PB-3 treats that answer as left.\n4. putTexts stops growing.\nThe note also states the client rule, the kernel scope (four derive files and no contract or validator change), and the 50-member acceptance bounds. The \"A repeat\" paragraph, decision 11, the section 8 line and O1 agree with section 3.9. The status line is accurate: current, amended, with the source head still to come.\n\nPlanner points (592a7ea8): Both are in section 3.9. (1) The late-open case says plainly that the O2 cutoff does not cover client acts. intent.notAfter bounds admission, and the ghost row lasts at most one lease. (2) The final-read audit names the map application, Pinboard, the shipped examples and apps, the client, the CLI and the MCP B4 projection. None reads final counts or live-items. The one test of live-items moves with the source head. The sibling repository names already appear in notes on main.\n\nArchitecture: Sound. Retained state now depends on open items and distinct keys, not on ticks. One behaviour change goes beyond the ruling text, and the note states it plainly: the live summary reports 0 for each final state, and the final-items read returns an empty complete page. A reader that counted departures from a live scope loses that count. The audit finds no such reader today, and at the live level an application that needs history records it. The source review checks that tests pin both answers.\nSecurity: No authority change. The retry record stays bound to the signing KeyId, and eviction removes only that item's records. A `no-item` answer to a stale act refuses the act and does not apply it.\nSimplification: One rule replaces a declared renewal form, and the validator does not change. No objection.\nWake rate: The note adds no alarm or timer (\"zero alarms added\"). Timed expiry keeps its existing timers. The wake floor is unchanged.\n\nFor the source head (not blocking this note): name the red witness for the fixed-hash claim in the review. Show the 10-versus-1,000 renewal byte equality and the churn return-to-total as measured runs, not projections. Add one test where one key acts on two items and retries the first.\n\nBinding: gs refused a delivery binding, because request 5fcd2b9b owes no Git artifact. This verdict is filed with --evidence-only. The content approval of the exact head stands. The landing route is the planner's to choose.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ba138bccbbba79fc8df7911f2a688c986fb36cab","binding":"evidence-only","head":"ed0775f3a3a4c5e184b109c4f1d32e34f11c76b4","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1fe9bfd8a5e41094c319e64a541245883a4653b0\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1fe9bfd8a5e41094c319e64a541245883a4653b0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}